@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · III · MAREN · THE RECORD AND HER DOMINION" m="TKC: TR · DOM; VOL. I · {v1:ardenne} · {v1:lived2}"
# Ashford and the hollows
plate: doc
dh: Covenant Registry | DOMINION OF ARDENNE · ASHFORD
df: Candidate | COLE, Maren · twenty-three
df: Nominated by | herself · four months of paperwork (TR)
df: Regional Assessment | second
df: Father | Crown officer, Ashford
df: Mother | from the mountain communities · came to Ashford at eighteen (TR)
stamp: COVENANT DAUGHTER
/end
rec:
Two worlds | One official, one quiet. She learned early that the difference between them mattered and could be dangerous (TR).
What she carries | Ashford sits close to classified operations in the outer territory. She absorbed the Empire's mountain work in fragments, not through access (TR).
Her Dominion | Ashford is the city the Empire keeps as proof Ardenne is pacified, and everything past the tree line says otherwise. The Ungoverned have their deepest roots in the hollows, where the mountain people call them something closer to saints (DOM).
In the Trials | Ardenne rarely sends a Covenant Daughter. When it does she's usually from Ashford, more Imperial than the hollows, and quiet about the gap (DOM).
prompt: The fragment she heard as a girl that she's been trying to understand ever since | fill

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · III · MAREN · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 1 OF 2" m="TKC: TR · DOM; VOL. I · {v1:ardenne} · {v1:lived2}"
# What she believes
rec:
Who taught her | An Ashford father in Crown service and a mother from the hollows (TR). INFERENCE: Two catechisms, one recited and one never written down.
What her mother's people practice | Marriage as a community declaration and a broom jumped. The First Winter Work, a real job in the community's survival at thirteen or fourteen. The Sitting, so the dead don't leave alone (DOM).
What she believes | OPEN QUESTION: Which of the two catechisms she reaches for when she's frightened.
empire: What the Temple teaches about a woman like her
Ashford's devotion is loud because watched people perform loyalty where it can be seen (DOM). POSSIBLE: The Temple teaches Ardenne girls Romans 13.1, "Let every soul be subject unto the higher powers," and calls the women in the hollows criminals.
/end
prompt: What her mother told her about the hollows, and what she left out | fill

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · III · MAREN · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 2 OF 2" m="2 KGS 5.2–3; 2 KGS 6.15–17; PS 121.1; ROM 13.1"
# The text
rec:
Her name | *Maren* has no biblical source. It's a Scandinavian form of Marina, "of the sea."
The servant girl · 2 Kings 5 | POSSIBLE: A captive girl from Israel tells her mistress the general could be healed by the prophet in Samaria. She knows something the powerful household doesn't. **Where it breaks:** Her knowledge sends a general to be healed. Maren's gets her left on a mountain.
Elisha's servant · 2 Kings 6 | POSSIBLE: Surrounded, the servant sees only the enemy, until his eyes are opened and "the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire" (6.17). **Where it breaks:** What's hidden in Maren's mountains belongs to the Empire.
tab:
| She'd quote | Never read to her |
| Psalm 121.1, "I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help" | 2 Kings 6.17, the mountain full of what you can't see |
box: Volume One
Ardenne, {v1:ardenne}. Lived religion, {v1:lived2}. Mountain, and the classified work, {v1:mountain}. Passages put to work, with Romans 13, {v1:put-to-work}.
/end

